  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening Resilience of Afghan Nationals and Host Communities in Pakistan through Multi-sectoral Interventions</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Instability in Afghanistan during the past few decades has led to a substantial influx of Afghans into Pakistan. Per current estimates, there are 3.7 million Afghans living in Pakistan. In this project, IOM is seeking to expand its support to vulnerable Afghan nationals in Pakistan and host communities to enhance their living conditions and resilience. This is being achieved through a set of activities centred around facilitating Afghans access to services through efforts to mitigate the tensions that might arise with the host community and through efforts targeting both the basic and longer-term needs of targeted populations. Adopting a community-owned approach and a holistic approach to meeting the multiple needs of affected populations, the activities engage humanitarian and development stakeholders, Government of Pakistan (GoP), local authorities, civil society, and beneficiaries themselves.</narrative>
  </description>
